<div id="intro" class="scroll-anchor"></div>

<p class="lead">
Latent Form Theory is a philosophy of making organized around three questions:
how form emerges, what materials already contain, and how perception allows
meaning to become visible.
</p>

<p>
The three volumes explore the relationship between reduction, material history,
and disciplined attention.
</p>

